From: Roger Pau Monne <roger@xenproject.org>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:02:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] x86/mm: take an extra page reference in p2m_add_foreign()
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

p2m_add_foreign() holds the domain's p2m lock when calling
guest_remove_page(), which inhibits the p2m TLB flush when
guest_remove_page() releases the gfn.  However p2m_add_foreign() does not
hold a reference to the removed page, and so the page is freed when
guest_remove_page() calls put_page() on it.  This is problematic, as the
page is freed before the p2m TLB is flushed.

Modify p2m_add_foreign() so it takes a reference to the page to be removed,
and make sure that reference is only dropped after the p2m lock has been
released.  Note the GFN to be removed needs to be unshared before the
reference is taken, as otherwise the call to get_page() would fail if the
entry is shared.

Also add an ASSERT() to ensure the function is called without the p2m being
already locked, so that we ensure the last put_gfn() in the function
performs a p2m flush if needed.

This is XSA-535 / CVE-2026-119783

Signed-off-by: Roger Pau Monné <roger@xenproject.org>
Acked-by: Jan Beulich <jbeulich@suse.com>
---
 xen/arch/x86/mm/p2m.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xen/arch/x86/mm/p2m.c b/xen/arch/x86/mm/p2m.c
index 588aedbb28bc..578d00ee3093 100644
--- a/xen/arch/x86/mm/p2m.c
+++ b/xen/arch/x86/mm/p2m.c
@@ -1910,10 +1910,12 @@ static int p2m_add_foreign(struct domain *tdom, unsigned long fgfn,
 {
     p2m_type_t p2mt, p2mt_prev;
     mfn_t prev_mfn, mfn;
-    struct page_info *page;
+    struct page_info *page, *prev_page = NULL;
     int rc;
     struct domain *fdom;
 
+    ASSERT(!p2m_locked_by_me(p2m_get_hostp2m(tdom)));
+
     if ( !arch_acquire_resource_check(tdom) )
         return -EPERM;
 
@@ -1953,15 +1955,30 @@ static int p2m_add_foreign(struct domain *tdom, unsigned long fgfn,
     mfn = page_to_mfn(page);
 
     /* Remove previously mapped page if it is present. */
-    prev_mfn = get_gfn(tdom, gpfn, &p2mt_prev);
+    prev_mfn = get_gfn_unshare(tdom, gpfn, &p2mt_prev);
+    if ( p2m_is_shared(p2mt_prev) )
+    {
+        rc = -ENOMEM;
+        goto put_both;
+    }
+
     if ( mfn_valid(prev_mfn) )
     {
         if ( is_special_page(mfn_to_page(prev_mfn)) )
             /* Special pages are simply unhooked from this phys slot */
             rc = p2m_remove_page(tdom, _gfn(gpfn), prev_mfn, 0);
         else
+        {
+            prev_page = mfn_to_page(prev_mfn);
+            if ( !get_page(prev_page, tdom) )
+            {
+                prev_page = NULL;
+                rc = -ENXIO;
+                goto put_both;
+            }
             /* Normal domain memory is freed, to avoid leaking memory. */
             rc = guest_remove_page(tdom, gpfn);
+        }
         if ( rc )
             goto put_both;
     }
@@ -1984,6 +2001,9 @@ static int p2m_add_foreign(struct domain *tdom, unsigned long fgfn,
      */
     put_gfn(tdom, gpfn);
 
+    if ( prev_page )
+        put_page(prev_page);
+
  put_one:
     put_page(page);
 
-- 
2.55.0

